{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1350372-the-weaver-and-wyld-as-enemies","id":1350372,"title":"The Weaver and Wyld as enemies","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","World of Darkness","Werewolf: The Apocalypse"],"posts":[{"date":"2019-11-22T19:46:56-08:00","id":1350372,"title":"The Weaver and Wyld as enemies","content":"Does anyone else think the weaver and wyld are downplayed a bit too much in WTA? I get that the wyrm is the more immediate antagonist of the garou, but it almost seems like some authors give the wyrm the combined powers of the entire triat as long as said powers are &quot;Bad&quot; in some way. <br /> <br /> Any ideas on how to adjust setting where the setting to less like the wyrm was the sole villain figure around which the setting revolves and more of a three way chess match between three players that nobody wants to win? how would you make keeping the wyld or weaver from taking over just as important to the setting?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T21:02:22-08:00","id":1350380,"title":"","content":"The Wyld is left out as the weakest of the three, but also the only one of the three that's still true to its initial role. The Wyld can be an antagonist easily enough, because it could push something that opposes the agenda of the PCs, but on the whole the Wyld doesn't have the capacity to actually keep itself oriented on a single goal long enough to become a major setting level antagonist. It's a force of nature and it's pretty much antithetical to the forces that drove the Weaver and Wyrm to fall from their initial positions.<br /> <br /> The Weaver is portrayed plenty as an enemy in the books even if the Wyrm is more in your face in the text. Nothing needs to change here, just how stress the bad stuff the Weaver is doing gets.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-22T22:22:11-08:00","id":1350388,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1350372-the-weaver-and-wyld-as-enemies?p=1350380#post1350380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Wyld is left out as the weakest of the three, but also the only one of the three that's still true to its initial role. The Wyld can be an antagonist easily enough, because it could push something that opposes the agenda of the PCs, but on the whole the Wyld doesn't have the capacity to actually keep itself oriented on a single goal long enough to become a major setting level antagonist. It's a force of nature and it's pretty much antithetical to the forces that drove the Weaver and Wyrm to fall from their initial positions.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'd argue it wouldn't have to be. The wyld is in a position where it can cause conflict simply by existing in a place. You could build entire stories around the wyld simply bleeding into areas at random, even areas like chernoble or the digital web. What the wyld has going for it is that it doesn't Need a massive, world-spanning plot to be relevant, it can cause conflict and wreck centuries-long plots(on all sides) by simply &quot;bleeding&quot; into the wrong place at the wrong time.<br /> <br /> Heck you can have garou pointing an laughing when a Wyld spirit storm rips into a Black spiral hive and turns it into Alice in Wonderland meets Hellraiser, only to come back home to find their caern in the same state. The Wyld isn't on anyone's side and no one can hope to predict or control it, they can only try to fight the current or hunker down until it passes. I feel that makes the wyld a wonderful potential antagonist if it just had a bit more presence.<br /> <br /> QUOTE=Heavy Arms;n1350380]The Weaver is portrayed plenty as an enemy in the books even if the Wyrm is more in your face in the text. Nothing needs to change here, just how stress the bad stuff the Weaver is doing gets.[/QUOTE]<br /> <br /> Yeah, but you don't see the weaver or a weaver plot as the central antagonist. I'm not looking to change the character as it were, just give it more screen time.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-23T02:27:44-08:00","id":1350407,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1350372-the-weaver-and-wyld-as-enemies?p=1350388#post1350388\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">I'd argue it wouldn't have to be.</div> </div> </div> </div>Sure. Nothing has to be the way it is in the setting.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> The wyld is in a position where it can cause conflict simply by existing in a place. </div> </div> </div>This is already the state of things.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> I feel that makes the wyld a wonderful potential antagonist if it just had a bit more presence. </div> </div> </div>The problem is that the more present that Wyld is, the harder it is to keep the setting coherent. However cool a Wyld incident might be, it can't keep happening without the setting falling apart. As well, having it strike too evenly makes it look more purposeful than it should be.<br /> <br /> It's also skipping that the Triat doesn't act directly. The Weaver and Wyrm don't come around and do stuff on Earth. Their minions do. That's why the Wyld doesn't do much on Earth. It can't keep a coherent organization of minions together to be a significant factor the way the other two can.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> Yeah, but you don't see the weaver or a weaver plot as the central antagonist. </div> </div> </div>I'm not sure that's really the case. It's just the more subtle of the two. Even the core books tend to note the dangers the Weaver represents, and most of the Garou Tribes are distinctly anit-Weaver even if less so than anti-Wyrm.<br /> <br /> It's also important to their respective roles. The Weaver is institutional and systematic problems where bad things happen in defense of the status quo. The Wyrm is the actively bad people doing bad things. Fighting Wyrm servants is, purposefully, &quot;easy.&quot; Fomori, Banes, and BSDs are bad. You kill them and move on. Fighting Weaver servants is harder. They blend into humanity better, they're persistent and hard to simply kill, and even if you do they can be so ubiquitous that it doesn't accomplish anything. <br /> <br /> The Weaver is also, on the surface, doing less immediately bad stuff. The Weaver allows the mass production of guns, which is something that's clearly not good by Garou values, but it's the Wyrm that's putting those guns in the hands of violent humans, fomori, and First Teams. Ignoring the Wyrm's minions doing direct and active harm to try to fight the Weaver's subtle presence is hard to justify.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/617-heavy-arms","name":"Heavy Arms","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar617_2.jpeg","title":"Banned","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"12634"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-11-30T20:36:02-08:00","id":1351959,"title":"","content":"You can alter the story with a perspective flip at any time and do a dramatic reveal that the weaver\u2019s insidious plans are worse than Pentex.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/19533-pnizzle","name":"Pnizzle","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar19533_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"383"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-09T20:56:40-08:00","id":1354055,"title":"","content":"One way to go about giving the Weaver a stronger villian role is to give it a group like pentex. A bad guy group you can sink your teeth in to (pun intended).<br /> <br /> Mage's technocracy can be great inspiration for this group especially the early books. You want to focus on Iteration X and the NWO (machine men with machine hearts all that). With all of their powers being Weaver spirit Gifts instead of you having to use an another power system. Just keep the core aesthetic in mind inhuman design, ultramodern technology, cold efficiency with no care for the hope or fears of humanity.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately I don't have any ideas for the Wyld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1685-looker","name":"Looker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T13:26:57-08:00","id":1354238,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Looker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1350372-the-weaver-and-wyld-as-enemies?p=1354055#post1354055\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">One way to go about giving the Weaver a stronger villian role is to give it a group like pentex. A bad guy group you can sink your teeth in to (pun intended).<br /> <br /> Mage's technocracy can be great inspiration for this group especially the early books. You want to focus on Iteration X and the NWO (machine men with machine hearts all that). With all of their powers being Weaver spirit Gifts instead of you having to use an another power system. Just keep the core aesthetic in mind inhuman design, ultramodern technology, cold efficiency with no care for the hope or fears of humanity.<br /> <br /> Unfortunately I don't have any ideas for the Wyld.</div> </div> </div> </div>Shinzui Industries already exists, though.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T14:30:26-08:00","id":1354243,"title":"","content":"Never heard of them before! Granted I\u2019m far from the world\u2019s biggest WTA fan but 2 people probably way bigger fans then me didn\u2019t even mention them so I don\u2019t feel all that bad about my ignorance. What information I could get on them began and ended with sparse wiki so I still think my advice would be useful in fleshing them out.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1685-looker","name":"Looker","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Dec 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"28"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T15:59:17-08:00","id":1354257,"title":"","content":"I'm inclined to view Werewolf's underlying three-part cosmic conflict as a game of Rock, Paper, Scissors. As conscripts of of the three components of the Triat, the Wyld, it figures that Werewolves would be directed by their spirit guides to focus more on fighting one opposing corner of the Triat over the other.<br /> <br /> If the totem spirits were to start warning the Garou that the Weaver is as much a threat as the Wyrm, it would herald a real crisis, as now two thirds of the Triat are presented as being calable of threatening the Wyld.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11599-reasor","name":"Reasor","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"693"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-10T20:29:56-08:00","id":1354291,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Looker</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1350372-the-weaver-and-wyld-as-enemies?p=1354243#post1354243\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Never heard of them before! Granted I\u2019m far from the world\u2019s biggest WTA fan but 2 people probably way bigger fans then me didn\u2019t even mention them so I don\u2019t feel all that bad about my ignorance. What information I could get on them began and ended with sparse wiki so I still think my advice would be useful in fleshing them out.</div> </div> </div> </div>They were sadly under-utilized, but if you want to use the Weaver as an antagonist, you probably have a copy of the Book of the Weaver, which describes them. DNA is also one of the established antagonists of the setting.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T13:32:27-08:00","id":1354443,"title":"","content":"Its also noted that the Weaver-Spirits can possess humans like Banes and turn them into Drones.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Jade Kingdom Warrior","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25523-shakanaka","name":"Shakanaka","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25523_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"951"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T13:59:28-08:00","id":1354452,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Shakanaka</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1350372-the-weaver-and-wyld-as-enemies?p=1354443#post1354443\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Its also noted that the Weaver-Spirits can possess humans like Banes and turn them into Drones.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not quite. Clarification by the OneSong is a much more involved process that can't be undone as easily - you can at least try to heal back the ten unsoakable levels of agg that a fomor gets when you rip the bane out with Exorcism or the like, but the weaver-spirit in a Drone is painstakingly fused together and worked into the host at every level.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-11T23:01:17-08:00","id":1354526,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Heavy Arms</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1350372-the-weaver-and-wyld-as-enemies?p=1350380#post1350380\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">The Weaver is portrayed plenty as an enemy in the books even if the Wyrm is more in your face in the text. Nothing needs to change here, just how stress the bad stuff the Weaver is doing gets.</div> </div> </div> </div>Hell, depending on which book you're reading, the Weaver is portrayed as more of the <i>real</i> enemy, while the Wyrm is the more <i>immediate</i> enemy. The Weaver's the reason the Wyrm was corrupted after all, and most of the biggest tools the forces of the Wyrm utilize have a heavy influence of things Weaver-like(big business and technology via Pentex being the most obvious).<br /> <br /> I don't think the Weaver's ever been portrayed as a non-threat or downplayed as a threat. Just, again, not as <i>immediate</i> of a threat. The Wyrm is the fire burning down your neighborhood. The Weaver is the arsonist who lit the fire.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>Writing up Clanbook: Aabbt","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/700-vysha","name":"Vysha","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar700_2.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"602"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-12T12:36:05-08:00","id":1354650,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Vysha</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1350372-the-weaver-and-wyld-as-enemies?p=1354526#post1354526\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> Hell, depending on which book you're reading, the Weaver is portrayed as more of the <i>real</i> enemy, while the Wyrm is the more <i>immediate</i> enemy. The Weaver's the reason the Wyrm was corrupted after all, and most of the biggest tools the forces of the Wyrm utilize have a heavy influence of things Weaver-like(big business and technology via Pentex being the most obvious).<br /> <br /> I don't think the Weaver's ever been portrayed as a non-threat or downplayed as a threat. Just, again, not as <i>immediate</i> of a threat. The Wyrm is the fire burning down your neighborhood. The Weaver is the arsonist who lit the fire.</div> </div> </div> </div>Maybe, but the wyrm is almost Always the immediate threat in any scenario to the point that you don't really see the other two. It also doesn't help that everything that's bad/wrong/gross/evil in some way is always attributed to being wyrmish or at least wyrm tainted, even if it doesn't make sense. The wyrm is the spirit of destruction, but for some reason can give gifts and fomori powers the having nothing to do with destruction in any way as long as they're &quot;Gross&quot; in some way.<br /> <br /> On the opposite end, I can't remember the last time I've ever seen the Wyld portrayed as an enemy. It's hyped up as supposedly being a threat just like the weaver and wyrm, but it never makes an appearance as an enemy and is even an ally sometimes. The time of judgement book had a scenario where the &quot;Good&quot; ending had the Wyld taking full power over the Entire tried, and they trumpeted that as a Good Thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T12:54:47-08:00","id":1355241,"title":"","content":"The Wyld is tricky to use as an antagonist because most of the time it showing up is a good thing by the morals of the Garou Nation, even if humanity would disagree. Certain garou would celebrate a hurricane leveling an entire shore line, while humans would naturally be horrified and distraught by the loss of development and life.<br /> <br /> The Wyld generally isn't the most directly antagonistic towards the Garou Nation although it could be. Agents of the Wyld could hypothetically attempt to whip the Red Talons and/or Black Furies into battle against Glass Walkers, Pentex, a random storefront, or whatever the heck that particular jaggling thinks is harming the Wyld atm. Ratkin could be great antagonists with their 'blow it up, ask questions never' mentality. Gorgons, rare as they are, could also be used to show how destructive and abnormal the Wyld is capable of being.<br /> <br /> The Weaver is more often portrayed as an antagonist, although it's true that Shenzui, DNA, and drones don't get nearly the amount of screen time that Black Spiral Dancers, Pentex, and Fomori do.<br /> <br /> Two of the really interesting things of the triat imo is that each aspect has a positive and negative aspect, even the Wyld whose brought up less. The Wyld is creative and innovative and is the breath of life, but it's also unpredictable and chaotic and as merciless as any force of nature. The Weaver is organized and stable and provides necessary structure, but it's also capable of becoming stagnant and tyrannical and unyielding in the face of reason or disaster. The Wyrm is cleansing and healthy yet has been driven mad and corruptive. Each is necessary and has elements that are both positive and negative for humanity and the Garou Nation.<br /> <br /> The other really interesting thing imo is how ultimately, despite their infighting, they still constantly feed into one another. Whenever the Wyld unleashes a hurricane, it might temporarily shatter some of the Weaver's creations and the Wyrm may revel in the destruction, but humanity is driven to rebuild and build better after the disaster. The Weaver can pave over a field but the Wyld will find news ways to spring up unless constantly fought back and the Wyrm may encourage it, as a victory of the Weaver only feeds it once. Each element of the triat is ultimately connected and the fact that they are fighting each other while simultaneously benefiting each other is a rather ironic sign of their insanity and kinda funny to me.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/11637-gryffon15","name":"Gryffon15","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar11637_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2016"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"900"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T12:59:05-08:00","id":1355244,"title":"","content":"The Book of the Wyld, naturally, had extensive notes on when the Wyld is not your friend, but since the Wyrm and Weaver get such top billing and two tribes in the core get billing as being champions of the Wyld, it gets pushed to the side more often than not. Some of the presentations included taking a cue from Day of the Triffids, with rampant growth of an alien organism threatening life on the planet, while another was that in addition to disasters, the boundaries between the physical world and Umbra began to unravel, with reality in threat of dissolution. Some of the gorgons introduced in the book helped that along, like Rorg's Hungry Children (living rocks that fall from space and eat human, but never wolf or Garou, flesh).","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T17:44:57-08:00","id":1355300,"title":"","content":"Imagine a sink; The Wyld is the pump, the weaver the pipes, the Wyrm the drain. The pipes and drainage make themselves as complicated as they can, the pump just continues to pump.<br /> I think a big mistake with werewolf is considering that the Triat are actually active. I don't think the any element of the Triat itself is actually trying to win, rather some high-level spirits who've indentified with the Triat are trying to win. It's less like there's three literal gods and more like three religions with lots of clergy who push for their faith's dominance, or three ideologies and several political parties that...<br /> <br /> The Garou are just half spirit; They don't know where &quot;The Wyrm&quot; as a concept splits from &quot;The Wyrm&quot; as a number of spirits. They're like employees who've never seen mid-level management, let along the top levels or even the company they're a subsidiary of.<br /> <br /> Go far enough and all the Triat is bad. It's just that the Wyrm's the most obvious bad. The Wyld's champions, by their very nature, aren't organizing much of a fight. The Wyrm is satisfying to fight in that it's all about justice, and the weaver is satisfying to fight in that it's <i>punk. </i>","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/25794-mywifeisscary","name":"MyWifeIsScary","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar25794_2.png","title":"Banned","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2019"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3711"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-16T18:22:57-08:00","id":1355309,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>MyWifeIsScary</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1350372-the-weaver-and-wyld-as-enemies?p=1355300#post1355300\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Imagine a sink; The Wyld is the pump, the weaver the pipes, the Wyrm the drain. The pipes and drainage make themselves as complicated as they can, the pump just continues to pump.<br /> I think a big mistake with werewolf is considering that the Triat are actually active. I don't think the any element of the Triat itself is actually trying to win, rather some high-level spirits who've indentified with the Triat are trying to win. It's less like there's three literal gods and more like three religions with lots of clergy who push for their faith's dominance, or three ideologies and several political parties that...<br /> <br /> The Garou are just half spirit; They don't know where &quot;The Wyrm&quot; as a concept splits from &quot;The Wyrm&quot; as a number of spirits. They're like employees who've never seen mid-level management, let along the top levels or even the company they're a subsidiary of.<br /> <br /> Go far enough and all the Triat is bad. It's just that the Wyrm's the most obvious bad. The Wyld's champions, by their very nature, aren't organizing much of a fight. The Wyrm is satisfying to fight in that it's all about justice, and the weaver is satisfying to fight in that it's <i>punk. </i></div> </div> </div> </div><br /> The pump can still be a problem if it refuses to *stop* pumping and keeps filling the kitchen until it floods out the house. The wyld also wouldn't really need to be organized, it's the vary concept of unexpected events and flipping the rules on their heads. A group of alley cats in boston could spontaneously become a pack of gorgons, start attacking a random shop behind a person doing a live news broadcast, and have the supernaturals from there to chicago would be scrambling to cover the breach of the veil/masquerade.<br /> <br /> I do believe the actual triat themselves can have agendas. The wyrm may be the living concept of entropy, but it's the Personified living concept of entropy. It can thus have all of the flaws and hang-ups that come with being a thinking being. Same applies to the rest of the triat.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-17T16:58:37-08:00","id":1355513,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1350372-the-weaver-and-wyld-as-enemies?p=1355309#post1355309\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> The pump can still be a problem if it refuses to *stop* pumping and keeps filling the kitchen until it floods out the house. The wyld also wouldn't really need to be organized, it's the vary concept of unexpected events and flipping the rules on their heads. A group of alley cats in boston could spontaneously become a pack of gorgons, start attacking a random shop behind a person doing a live news broadcast, and have the supernaturals from there to chicago would be scrambling to cover the breach of the veil/masquerade.<br /> <br /> I do believe the actual triat themselves can have agendas. The wyrm may be the living concept of entropy, but it's the Personified living concept of entropy. It can thus have all of the flaws and hang-ups that come with being a thinking being. Same applies to the rest of the triat.</div> </div> </div> </div>It's rather misleading to try and use the Mage label. It's a manifestation of either Destruction or Corruption; entropy isn't even really close, since it tends to favor creating more degrees of freedom, which is Wyld-ish, and I know I'm in strained territory here but WW could really have done with better reading on what entropy was back in the day.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T15:17:33-08:00","id":1355699,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Saur Ops Specialist</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1350372-the-weaver-and-wyld-as-enemies?p=1355513#post1355513\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> It's rather misleading to try and use the Mage label. It's a manifestation of either Destruction or Corruption; entropy isn't even really close, since it tends to favor creating more degrees of freedom, which is Wyld-ish, and I know I'm in strained territory here but WW could really have done with better reading on what entropy was back in the day.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> Entropy isn't a mage label. It's a concept of thermodynamics that states that no system is perfect and thus all systems gradually &quot;leak&quot; energy until they don't function properly anymore.<br /> <br /> I.E. It breaks everything that exists so that new things can exist by using the newly freed energy.<br /> <br /> Mage stole the word and uses it improperly. White-wolf isn't very good at being accurate when it comes to culture or science.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6383-prometheas","name":"Prometheas","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1101"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2019-12-18T16:17:39-08:00","id":1355713,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prometheas</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/werewolf-the-apocalypse-aa/1350372-the-weaver-and-wyld-as-enemies?p=1355699#post1355699\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> <br /> Entropy isn't a mage label. It's a concept of thermodynamics that states that no system is perfect and thus all systems gradually &quot;leak&quot; energy until they don't function properly anymore.<br /> <br /> I.E. It breaks everything that exists so that new things can exist by using the newly freed energy.<br /> <br /> Mage stole the word and uses it improperly. White-wolf isn't very good at being accurate when it comes to culture or science.</div> </div> </div> </div>I know. I was complaining about the same thing.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/23-saur-ops-specialist","name":"Saur Ops Specialist","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar23_3.png","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"9371"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}